-- Seed: new surface_finishes + appliance_catalog_items rows
-- Generated by scripts/seed_finishes_and_appliances.mjs — safe to re-run (ON CONFLICT upserts).

-- Physical-scale / relief / tiling-mode correction for the 12 ambientCG-backed
-- rows below (finish_wood_* through finish_tile_*), 2026-09-05.
--
-- swatch_width_mm/swatch_height_mm: previously a copy-pasted placeholder
-- unrelated to the actual scan. Real per-asset values pulled from
-- https://ambientcg.com/api/v2/full_json?id=<assetId> (dimensionX/dimensionY,
-- in cm, converted to mm below) where the API returned a nonzero value;
-- ambientCG does not record physical size for every asset, so some rows fall
-- back to the estimate table from the task brief. Each row below is marked
-- VERIFIED (from the API) or ESTIMATED (fallback table) — do not treat an
-- ESTIMATED value as measured.
--   finish_wood_dark_walnut         VERIFIED  Wood051 dimensionX/Y=80cm  -> 800x800mm
--   finish_wood_plywood_edge        ESTIMATED Chipboard004 API dimension=0 (unset)
--   finish_wood_reclaimed           VERIFIED  Wood066 dimensionX/Y=40cm  -> 400x400mm
--   finish_stone_black_granite      ESTIMATED Granite002A API dimension=0 (unset)
--   finish_stone_white_quartz       ESTIMATED Marble021 API dimension=0 (unset)
--   finish_stone_concrete           VERIFIED  Concrete034 dimensionX/Y=110/55cm -> 1100x550mm
--                                   (matches the on-disk 1024x512 2:1 image; old
--                                   1000x1000 was squashing it to 1:1)
--   finish_metal_brushed_steel      ESTIMATED Metal050A API dimension=0 (unset)
--   finish_metal_polished_chrome    ESTIMATED Metal032 API dimension=0 (unset)
--   finish_metal_matte_black        ESTIMATED Metal046A API dimension=0 (unset)
--   finish_metal_brushed_brass      ESTIMATED Metal048A API dimension=0 (unset)
--   finish_tile_large_ceramic_floor VERIFIED  Tiles141 dimensionX/Y=200cm -> 2000x2000mm
--                                   (whole-texture size from the API; a visual
--                                   count of the image gives a 6x6 tile grid,
--                                   i.e. ~333mm/tile, consistent with a large
--                                   floor tile — used the verified whole-image
--                                   value directly rather than re-deriving it)
--   finish_tile_moroccan_geometric  ESTIMATED Tiles138 API dimension=0 (unset);
--                                   counted a 12x12 grid of tiles in the image,
--                                   fallback table says one tile = 200mm, so
--                                   swatch = 12 * 200mm = 2400x2400mm
--
-- relief_strength: was a blanket 0.3 on every row regardless of material.
-- Replaced with per-material values (all 12 rows already have a real
-- normal_map_url, so this is scaling an authored map via reliefToNormalScale,
-- not deriving one from luminance): near-zero for metals and polished stone
-- (~0.03-0.08, low but nonzero so the real normal map's brush/pit detail
-- still reads), moderate for concrete (~0.35-0.4 per PATTERN_RELIEF_PRESET),
-- and strong for the wood and tile rows (~0.65-0.75 — tile grout lines are
-- genuinely recessed, closer to wood's 0.7 preset than to stone's).
--
-- tiling_mode: was 'mirror' on every row. These are ambientCG scans, which
-- tile seamlessly by construction — 'mirror' exists for photographed
-- swatches that don't tile (e.g. a business's own phone photo) and only
-- costs visible symmetry here for no benefit. Set to 'repeat'.
